menu "Delta Omega User Behaviors"

config ZMK_RAPID_FIRE_MIN_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Rapid-fire minimum interval in milliseconds"
    default 20
    range 5 1000

config ZMK_RAPID_FIRE_MAX_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Rapid-fire maximum interval in milliseconds"
    default 26
    range 5 1000

config ZMK_RAPID_FIRE_TAP_MS
    int "Rapid-fire virtual tap duration in milliseconds"
    default 2
    range 1 100
    help
      A 1ms virtual press is only as wide as a single USB 1000Hz polling
      frame, leaving no margin for the host to reliably observe it. 2ms
      costs nothing against the 20-26ms interval (repeat rate is set by
      the interval, not this) but gives a full frame of headroom.

config ZMK_DEBOUNCE_TAP_COOLDOWN_MS
    int "Debounce-tap: minimum gap between fires on the same position"
    default 30
    range 5 200
    help
      A repeat trigger on the same position within this window of the
      last one is treated as switch chatter and ignored.

config ZMK_DEBOUNCE_TAP_MS
    int "Debounce-tap: virtual tap duration in milliseconds"
    default 5
    range 1 100

config ZMK_SPACE_HT_TAPPING_TERM_MS
    int "Space hold-tap: tapping term in milliseconds"
    default 190
    range 50 500

config ZMK_SPACE_HT_RELEASE_GRACE_MS
    int "Space hold-tap: grace period after release before deactivating the hold layer"
    default 40
    range 5 200
    help
      If the key is pressed again within this window after releasing
      while the hold layer is active, the release is treated as switch
      chatter and the hold continues uninterrupted.

config ZMK_GAMING_CMD_WINDOW_MS
    int "Gaming command state machine: window to remember a pending Down-arrow sequence"
    default 220
    range 50 2000
    help
      How long the internal state machine remembers a pending down-arrow
      -> down-arrow sequence (Command A/B on the Gaming layer) before
      auto-resetting to idle. This only bounds how long the *state* is
      remembered - every physical press still outputs its HID key
      immediately, nothing is buffered or delayed.

config ZMK_G_LATCH_MAX_HOLD_MS
    int "G latch: maximum total HID hold duration in milliseconds"
    default 180
    range 50 2000
    help
      Experimental rapid-fire alternative for a single key (glatch
      branch only). G's HID stays down after physical release (latched)
      until a direction key (LEFT/RIGHT) ends it or this many ms have
      elapsed since the *physical press* - whichever comes first. Not an
      extra delay added after release; it's a cap on total HID hold time
      from press. A/B candidates: 150/180/220.

endmenu
